  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 116 PM EDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nQuieter weather expected this afternoon and evening with clouds \nstill slowly clearing out. This cloud deck has helped keep \ntemperatures in check today with many locations still sitting in the \nlow 80's as of this writing. Those locations in the southern Valley \nthat have cleared out are really ramping up in temperature \nhowever... Clouds will eventually clear out, and unfortunately \neveryone will get another warm day today like most days the past \nmonth. \n\nA shortwave will move through to our north tomorrow, followed by a \nsurface cold front. CAMs generally have no PoPs associated with this \ndry front with the better forcing remaining off to our north. Can't \ncompletely rule out a few isolated showers, but it looks \nincreasingly unlikely. Front eventually moves through, but it's more \nof a front in name, rather than impact as we should get yet another \nvery warm day across the eastern Tennessee Valley.\n\nThe dog days of summer are back in full effect Tuesday through the \nend of the week with highs in the 90's for most of the Valley \nlocations... and Heat Index values eclipsing the triple digit mark \nfor most people along I-40 and south. We could see multiple days of \nHeat Advisories needed on Tuesday and beyond. Dew point values are \nforecasted to drop a couple of degrees by the second half of the \nweek, so we might \"technically\" not hit Heat Advisory criteria... \nbut we'll almost certainly be within a few degrees of it. Any way \nyou slice it this upcoming week is shaping up to be hot and mostly \ndry again.",
